i.push(n.kt("We collect the following types of information to provide and improve our services:\n\n\u2022 Account Information: Name, email address, phone number, and profile details provided during registration.\n\u2022 Authentication Data: Firebase Authentication manages your login credentials securely.\n\u2022 Transaction History: Records of rewards earned, withdrawals made, and referral activities.\n\u2022 Device Information: Device type, operating system, and unique device identifiers for fraud prevention.\n\u2022 Ad Interaction Data: Ad views and interactions for analytics and reward calculation.",k,"1. Information We Collect"))
i.push(n.kt("Fun Pay uses the following Firebase services, operated by Google LLC:\n\n\u2022 Firebase Authentication: Manages user registration and secure login. We store your email, hashed password, and phone number.\n\u2022 Cloud Firestore: Stores user profiles, wallet balances, reward history, referral data, and consent agreements.\n\u2022 Firebase Cloud Messaging: Sends push notifications about rewards, withdrawals, and account updates.\n\u2022 Firebase Crashlytics: Collects crash reports and performance data to improve app stability.\n\nFor more information on how Firebase processes data, visit the Google Privacy Policy.",k,"2. Firebase Services"))
i.push(n.kt("Fun Pay integrates Google AdMob to serve rewarded video ads. AdMob may collect:\n\n\u2022 Device advertising identifiers (e.g., Google Advertising ID)\n\u2022 IP address and device location (approximate)\n\u2022 Ad interaction data (views, clicks, engagement)\n\nAdMob uses this data to deliver relevant ads and measure ad performance. You can opt out of interest-based advertising through your device settings. By using Fun Pay, you consent to AdMob's data collection as described in Google's Privacy Policy.",k,"3. AdMob Advertising"))
i.push(n.kt("We use Google AdSense to serve advertisements on the Fun Pay website. Google, as a third-party vendor, uses cookies to serve ads on this site.\n\n\u2022 Google's use of the DART cookie enables it to serve ads to users based on their visits to this site and other sites on the Internet.\n\u2022 Users may opt out of the use of the DART cookie by visiting the Google ad and content network privacy policy at https://policies.google.com/technologies/ads.\n\u2022 You can opt out of some third-party vendor's use of cookies for interest-based advertising by visiting aboutads.info.\n\nThird-party vendors, including Google, use cookies to serve ads based on a user's prior visits to this website or other websites. This Privacy Policy covers the use of cookies by Fun Pay and does not cover the use of cookies by any advertisers.",k,"3a. Google AdSense & Cookies"))
i.push(n.kt("Fun Pay operates a rewards-based system where users earn rewards for:\n\n\u2022 Watching rewarded video advertisements\n\u2022 Completing daily check-ins and maintaining streaks\n\u2022 Completing tasks and challenges\n\u2022 Referring new users to the platform\n\nReward data (type, amount, timestamps) is stored in Firestore to track your earnings. Referral information is recorded to verify legitimate referrals and prevent abuse.",k,"4. User Rewards System"))
i.push(n.kt("We use your information to:\n\n\u2022 Operate, maintain, and improve Fun Pay\n\u2022 Process and track rewards, withdrawals, and referral bonuses\n\u2022 Detect, prevent, and investigate fraudulent or prohibited activities\n\u2022 Send notifications about rewards, account updates, and policy changes\n\u2022 Comply with legal obligations and enforce our Terms & Conditions",k,"5. How We Use Your Information"))
i.push(n.kt("We implement industry-standard security measures to protect your data:\n\n\u2022 Encryption in Transit: All data transmitted between the app and Firebase is encrypted using TLS/SSL.\n\u2022 Encryption at Rest: Data stored in Firestore is encrypted using AES-256.\n\u2022 Firebase Security Rules: Access to Firestore documents is restricted based on user authentication and data ownership.\n\u2022 Secure Authentication: Passwords are never stored in plain text; Firebase handles hashing and salting.\n\u2022 Fraud Monitoring: Automated systems monitor for suspicious activity to protect user accounts.",k,"6. Data Security"))
i.push(n.kt("We do not sell your personal information to third parties. Data may be shared with:\n\n\u2022 Firebase (Google): For authentication, database, notifications, and crash reporting.\n\u2022 Google AdMob: For serving advertisements.\n\u2022 Law Enforcement: If required by law or to protect our legal rights.\n\nAll third-party service providers are contractually obligated to protect your data.",k,"7. Data Sharing and Third Parties"))
i.push(n.kt("You have the following rights regarding your personal data:\n\n\u2022 Access: View your account data anytime in the app.\n\u2022 Update: Edit your profile information in Settings.\n\u2022 Export: Request a copy of your data by contacting us.\n\u2022 Delete: Delete your account and associated data through the Profile screen.\n\u2022 Withdraw Consent: Uninstall the app and contact us to request data removal.",k,"8. Your Rights"))
i.push(n.kt("You can delete your account at any time through the Profile screen in the app. Upon account deletion:\n\n\u2022 Your profile, wallet, and reward data will be permanently removed from Firestore within 30 days.\n\u2022 Transaction records may be retained for legal and compliance purposes.\n\u2022 Firebase Authentication account will be deleted.\n\u2022 Any pending withdrawals will be cancelled.",k,"9. Account Deletion"))
i.push(n.kt("Fun Pay is not intended for users under 13 years of age. We do not knowingly collect personal information from children under 13. If we discover that a child under 13 has provided us with personal data, we will take steps to delete that information immediately.",k,"10. Children's Privacy"))
i.push(n.kt("We may update this Privacy Policy from time to time. Users will be notified of material changes via in-app notification or email. Continued use of Fun Pay after changes constitutes acceptance of the updated policy. We encourage you to review this page periodically.",k,"11. Changes to This Policy"))
i.push(n.kt("For privacy-related inquiries, data requests, or questions about this policy, please contact us:\n\nEmail: jagadeeshmurthym4@gmail.com\nOr visit the Contact Us page in the app.",k,"12. Contact Us"))
